      "mergedPostDetails": "With the Quest2's past updates we've seen some very impressive hand tracking through the built in cameras. you can use this easily in VRchat already, but the hands still mimic the normal controllers (ie. no individual finger tracking or splaying)\nI propose vrchat should be able to read the full hand and finger tracking data the quest2 creates and display it.\nThe advantages of this is adding a ton of communication options, splaying fingers and hand signals are important in communication as well as sign language, and a majority of users already have the technology built in (like 70% of steam vr is quest-quest2 users)\nas said earlier, it's almost already like this in game, adding the extra bit of tracking would greatly improve immersion, conversation, and language. \nthanks for reading and I really hope you guys consider this",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Oculus hand tracking",
