      "mergedPostDetails": "Rift Finger tracking has always been a thing. In this video, I demonstrate how the oculus controllers work using their full potential. This is recorded in Gmod VR using a community made mod. https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/514549575969931264/644585848439832576/VRMod.mp4 You can move your index finger on it's own, your thumb on it's own, and the middle, ring, and pinkie as one, individual from the index, and thumb; all of which use their respective analog controls. (I fixed the wording. Hopefully that helps.)\n\nI think it would be a really cool feature to implement!  \nFrom what I can tell, SteamVR already implements this. Either the devs changed this in SteamVR or much more complicated, it was reworked along-side the vive using unity. I believe it's the ladder mostly because any changes I make in SteamVR do not affect the analog controls VRChat has. \n\nYeah, Rift CV1 is gone, but the rift S and Quest use the same controllers and they work the same for the most part.",
